---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/about.scss"
import download from "../assets/images/icons/download.png";
import email from "../assets/images/icons/email.png";
import linkedin from "../assets/images/icons/linkedin.png";
import bg from "../assets/images/contact-bg.svg";
---
<BaseLayout
        title="About me"
        bg={bg}
>
    <main class="container about-page" id="main-content">
        <article class="case-study">
            <div class="row justify-content-between">
            <div class="col-md-7">

            <section class="hero hero--project hero--project--uchicago">

                <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
                    <h1 class="hero--project__description ">Curiosity is at the heart of how I
                        work</h1>
                </div>

                <p class="hero--project__summary ">
                    I’m Aga Domańska, a product designer for complex, information-rich
                    products, with particular experience in research and open knowledge.
                    I combine user research, workflow and interaction design, accessibility
                    and technical understanding to shape products from their earliest
                    questions through to working interfaces.
                </p>
            </section>
                    <section class="about-page__section ">
                        <h2>From implementation to product design</h2>

                        <p>
                            My route into product design began in software development and front-end
                            engineering. As my work brought me closer to users and clients, I became
                            increasingly interested not only in how an interface should be built, but
                            why it should take a particular shape in the first place.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            That technical background still influences how I design. I understand
                            implementation constraints, prototype with real behaviour in mind and can
                            translate design decisions into detailed, accessible requirements. I work
                            comfortably with developers, but I also know when a technical limitation
                            should be accepted, questioned or solved differently.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section class="about-page__section ">
                        <h2>Learning from people who know their subject</h2>

                        <p>
                            I love knowledge: how it is discovered, organised, challenged and shared.
                            Science and research fascinate me, but so do the people behind them. Some
                            of the most rewarding parts of my work are conversations with researchers
                            and subject experts—people who have spent years understanding something
                            deeply and are generous enough to help the rest of us understand it better.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            My role is not to become the expert in every subject. It is to listen
                            closely, ask useful questions and uncover how that expertise needs to work
                            within a product. I enjoy turning specialist language, complicated
                            relationships and partly unspoken working practices into something that
                            other people can navigate and use.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section class="about-page__section ">
                        <h2>Making complexity workable</h2>

                        <p>
                            I am drawn to products where the difficulty cannot simply be removed:
                            interconnected metadata, specialist editorial decisions, conditional
                            workflows and large amounts of information. My job is to find the
                            structure within that complexity without oversimplifying the subject itself.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            I work closely with users, clients and developers throughout the process.
                            I clarify requirements, map workflows, test assumptions and consider the
                            states and exceptions that are easy to miss. Accessibility is part of that
                            work from the beginning—not a final compliance check. Semantic structure,
                            keyboard behaviour, cognitive load and clear language all contribute to
                            whether a product genuinely works for the people who need it.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            The result I aim for is not merely a polished interface. It is a product
                            whose behaviour makes sense, whose decisions can be explained and whose
                            implementation supports the people it was designed for.
                        </p>
                    </section>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <section class="about-page__section about-page__contact " style="margin-top: 6rem;">
                        <h2  id="contact">Let’s talk</h2>

                        <p>
                            If you are working on a complex product and need someone who can move
                            comfortably between users, specialist knowledge, design and implementation,
                            I would be glad to hear about it.
                        </p>

                        <div class="links" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
                            <a href="mailto:aga.domanska.design@gmail.com">
                                <img src={email.src} alt="" class="email-icon"/>
                                <strong>aga.domanska.design [at] gmail.com</strong>
                            </a>
                            <a class="linkedin" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/amdomanska" target="_blank"
                               rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                <img src={linkedin.src} alt="" class="linkedin_icon"/>
                                <strong>LinkedIn</strong>
                            </a>
                            <a href="/ADomanska-CV.pdf" type="application/pdf" target="_blank">
                                <img
                                        src={download.src}
                                        alt=""
                                        class="download"
                                />
                                <strong>Download CV</strong>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>